---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import linalg from '../courses/linear-algebra/meta.json';
import prob from '../courses/probability/meta.json';
import calc from '../courses/calculus/meta.json';
import opt from '../courses/optimization/meta.json';
import exam from '../courses/exam-review/meta.json';
---
<Base title="PrepUSI · Study Hub">

<div class="topbar">
  <span class="brand">PREPUSI · STUDY HUB</span>
  <span class="tag">MSc Finance · Assessment</span>
  <div class="right">
    <button id="themebtn">◐ theme: dark</button>
  </div>
</div>

<main class="home">
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="bar"><span class="pill g">v1.0</span><span>Course library ⟶ pick a course</span><span class="ctl" style="margin-left:auto;color:var(--dim)">⊡ ✕</span></div>
    <div class="body" style="grid-template-columns:1fr">
      <div>
        <h1>Study Hub</h1>
        <p>Cheat sheets for the MSc Finance assessment. Each course: definitions, key theorems, worked examples at exam level, and the traps examiners like. The exam review works back through the actual self-assessment paper.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <a class="course-card" href="/exam-review">
    <div class="panel" style="margin-bottom:0">
      <div class="bar"><span class="pill a">EXAM</span> Prep Exam Review<span class="ctl">— ⊡ ✕</span></div>
      <div class="body">
        <p>{exam.stats}</p>
        <p class="muted">The summer self-assessment, question by question. Part 1: moments and co-movement — pmf → expected value → variance → linear transformations → covariance → sums and differences → independence → products, then the six questions solved in full.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </a>

  <a class="course-card" href="/refresher">
    <div class="panel" style="margin-bottom:0">
      <div class="bar"><span class="pill g">NEW</span> Refresher Course<span class="ctl">— ⊡ ✕</span></div>
      <div class="body">
        <p>3 parts · fundamentals, linear algebra, probability · built lecture by lecture</p>
        <p class="muted">The USI Refresher Course in Mathematics and Probability, following the slide decks in order and solving every exercise in them. Parts 2 (Linear Algebra, 14 modules) and 3 (Probability, 18 modules) are live — matrices, vector spaces and linear systems; then sets, axioms, random variables, distributions, joint behaviour and tail risk.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </a>

  <a class="course-card" href="/linear-algebra">
    <div class="panel" style="margin-bottom:0">
      <div class="bar"><span class="pill g">LIVE</span> Linear Algebra<span class="ctl">— ⊡ ✕</span></div>
      <div class="body">
        <p>{linalg.stats}</p>
        <p class="muted">Vectors → matrices → linear systems → determinants → eigenvalues → quadratic forms → orthogonality → finance applications.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </a>

  <a class="course-card" href="/probability">
    <div class="panel" style="margin-bottom:0">
      <div class="bar"><span class="pill g">LIVE</span> Probability<span class="ctl">— ⊡ ✕</span></div>
      <div class="body">
        <p>{prob.stats}</p>
        <p class="muted">Counting → conditional probability → random variables → expectation → distributions → joint behaviour → limit theorems → finance applications.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </a>

  <a class="course-card" href="/calculus">
    <div class="panel" style="margin-bottom:0">
      <div class="bar"><span class="pill g">LIVE</span> Calculus<span class="ctl">— ⊡ ✕</span></div>
      <div class="body">
        <p>{calc.stats}</p>
        <p class="muted">Functions → limits → continuity → derivatives → curve study → integrals → techniques → partial derivatives → multiple integrals → finance applications.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </a>

  <a class="course-card" href="/optimization">
    <div class="panel" style="margin-bottom:0">
      <div class="bar"><span class="pill g">LIVE</span> Optimization<span class="ctl">— ⊡ ✕</span></div>
      <div class="body">
        <p>{opt.stats}</p>
        <p class="muted">The problem → one variable → convexity → first- and second-order conditions → global optima → the Lagrange method → shadow prices → inequality constraints → portfolio theory.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </a>
</main>

<script>
  import '../scripts/course.js';
</script>
</Base>
